1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:05,985
<i>I see.</i>

2
00:00:06,069 --> 00:00:07,362
<i>Orange peels…</i>

3
00:00:07,445 --> 00:00:10,115
<i>-If you want, we can make them together.</i>
<i>-No, I can't do it.</i>

4
00:00:10,198 --> 00:00:11,533
<i>You can!</i>

5
00:00:12,867 --> 00:00:15,120
<i>I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.</i>

6
00:00:15,203 --> 00:00:17,163
You're interested in Midori, aren't you?

7
00:00:17,247 --> 00:00:19,082
<i>But she probably…</i>

8
00:00:19,165 --> 00:00:21,084
<i>Do you think we can be a couple?</i>

9
00:00:21,167 --> 00:00:25,463
"A woman's heart
is a deep ocean of secrets."

10
00:00:25,547 --> 00:00:27,215
<i>Mr. Nishigami…</i>

11
00:00:27,298 --> 00:00:29,217
<i>Do you have a girlfriend?</i>

12
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:31,886
No. I have no one like that.

13
00:00:31,970 --> 00:00:34,973
I may be falling in love
for the first time!

14
00:00:35,807 --> 00:00:39,185
<i>You're getting friendly again</i>
<i>with those people.</i>

15
00:00:39,269 --> 00:00:40,103
<i>Given your position,</i>

16
00:00:40,186 --> 00:00:43,189
<i>falling in love with a human</i>
<i>is out of the question.</i>

17
00:00:43,273 --> 00:00:45,692
Be careful on your way home.
See you tomorrow.

18
00:00:47,151 --> 00:00:48,361
See you tomorrow.

19
00:00:52,532 --> 00:00:54,159
TWO DAYS LATER

20
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:18,266
Veggies first.

21
00:01:18,349 --> 00:01:19,726
Yeah, veggies first.

22
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:21,144
-Is this crab paste?
-Yummy.

23
00:01:21,227 --> 00:01:22,395
-It's good.
-Crab paste?

24
00:01:22,478 --> 00:01:24,272
-Oh, this is crab paste.
-Really?

25
00:01:24,981 --> 00:01:26,149
It's crab paste.

26
00:01:26,232 --> 00:01:27,275
-Try it.
-I will.

27
00:01:27,358 --> 00:01:28,735
It's like regular mayonnaise.

28
00:01:28,818 --> 00:01:30,570
Really? It tastes like crab paste.

29
00:01:31,112 --> 00:01:32,363
Yeah, it's crab paste.

30
00:01:32,447 --> 00:01:34,365
-It is.
-Thank you for the meal.

31
00:01:35,575 --> 00:01:36,910
Oh, it's fine. Leave it there.

32
00:01:36,993 --> 00:01:37,952
I'll wash it.

33
00:01:38,036 --> 00:01:39,120
Thank you.

34
00:01:39,203 --> 00:01:40,121
Good night.

35
00:01:40,204 --> 00:01:41,873
Good night!

36
00:01:45,168 --> 00:01:46,961
I wonder what happened to Midori?

37
00:01:47,045 --> 00:01:49,047
She's been down these past two days.

38
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:50,632
Did she get sick or something?

39
00:01:50,715 --> 00:01:52,300
Huh? I didn't notice at all.

40
00:01:52,967 --> 00:01:55,094
Konta, how dense can you be?

41
00:01:55,178 --> 00:01:56,971
What? Did something happen to her?

42
00:01:58,097 --> 00:01:59,933
-Right?
-Yeah.

43
00:02:00,016 --> 00:02:01,392
What is it?

44
00:02:01,476 --> 00:02:04,646
She's probably down because
Mr. Nishigami hasn't been coming.

45
00:02:05,396 --> 00:02:06,314
What?

46
00:02:08,775 --> 00:02:11,361
Hey, Midori, seriously?

47
00:02:11,444 --> 00:02:12,487
Is that how it is?

48
00:02:13,196 --> 00:02:15,406
So she…

49
00:02:16,908 --> 00:02:18,326
and Mr. Nishigami?

50
00:02:18,993 --> 00:02:20,078
Are they…

51
00:02:20,161 --> 00:02:21,412
a couple yet?

52
00:02:22,038 --> 00:02:23,706
It's finally here.

53
00:02:23,790 --> 00:02:25,875
Midori's first love.

54
00:02:25,959 --> 00:02:27,585
That's certainly what it is.

55
00:02:27,669 --> 00:02:31,047
Still, Mr. Nishigami hasn't come
for the past two days.

56
00:02:31,130 --> 00:02:32,715
Why is that? Why isn't he coming?

57
00:02:32,799 --> 00:02:34,133
No idea, seriously.

58
00:02:34,217 --> 00:02:36,302
-He used to come almost every day.
-Right?

59
00:02:36,386 --> 00:02:38,388
Hey, the last time he came,

60
00:02:38,471 --> 00:02:40,974
he and Midori were making
orange peels together, right?

61
00:02:41,057 --> 00:02:42,350
Did something happen then?

62
00:02:42,433 --> 00:02:44,477
They were having fun!
Which is why it's strange.

63
00:02:44,560 --> 00:02:48,022
Right? So what's up with Mr. Nishigami?

64
00:02:48,106 --> 00:02:50,650
He isn't playing
with Midori's feelings, right?

65
00:02:50,733 --> 00:02:53,778
Well, I wonder.

66
00:02:53,861 --> 00:02:54,988
What should we do?

67
00:02:55,071 --> 00:02:56,990
I mean, is Midori even aware of it?

68
00:02:57,073 --> 00:02:58,700
Of her own love.

69
00:02:58,783 --> 00:03:00,827
No idea.

70
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:02,787
She's the sister of that idiot, after all.

71
00:03:02,870 --> 00:03:03,997
Idiot?

72
00:03:04,080 --> 00:03:06,082
Konta is an idiot, but a cute one!

73
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:08,918
Sure. And are you hooking up
with that idiot?

74
00:03:09,002 --> 00:03:11,045
Nope. We're not dating yet.

75
00:03:11,129 --> 00:03:12,797
Right now, I'm making him chase me.

76
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:16,843
Well, whatever.
Right now, it's about Midori.

77
00:03:16,926 --> 00:03:17,802
What do we do?

78
00:03:17,885 --> 00:03:20,221
But, you know Midori's personality.

79
00:03:20,304 --> 00:03:23,891
If we say something like,
"You like Mr. Nishigami, don't you?"

80
00:03:23,975 --> 00:03:25,435
She won't admit it.

81
00:03:25,518 --> 00:03:27,145
Well, yeah.

82
00:03:27,228 --> 00:03:30,231
Her dating experience
is like a middle schooler's.

83
00:03:30,857 --> 00:03:32,859
For now, let's wait and see.

84
00:03:32,942 --> 00:03:34,861
Tetsuro needs to do his best.

85
00:03:34,944 --> 00:03:36,321
Huh, Tetsuro?

86
00:03:36,404 --> 00:03:37,947
Why is he relevant here?

87
00:03:38,031 --> 00:03:40,325
That guy is crazy about Midori.

88
00:03:40,408 --> 00:03:41,367
What?

89
00:03:41,951 --> 00:03:45,246
It seems he hasn't even realized
his own feelings, though.

90
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:48,416
We have too many love novices here.

91
00:03:48,499 --> 00:03:50,001
It makes me laugh.

92
00:03:50,084 --> 00:03:54,047
Spoken like an expert.
A girl with a clingy ex.

93
00:03:54,839 --> 00:03:55,882
What?

94
00:03:55,965 --> 00:03:57,133
How did you know that?

95
00:03:57,216 --> 00:04:00,595
Your ex looked
at your social media followers,

96
00:04:00,678 --> 00:04:02,805
found me, and sent me a message.

97
00:04:03,473 --> 00:04:06,768
He said, "I want to get back
with Tsumugi, so please persuade her."

98
00:04:06,851 --> 00:04:08,686
How gross!

99
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:13,399
I'm sure he saw photos and videos
of you having fun at this villa,

100
00:04:13,483 --> 00:04:16,110
so he wants to have fun with you again.

101
00:04:17,487 --> 00:04:20,365
Well, it's true that
back when I was with him,

102
00:04:20,448 --> 00:04:23,368
before coming here, I didn't smile much.

103
00:04:23,451 --> 00:04:24,285
Yeah.

104
00:04:24,369 --> 00:04:27,163
Since coming to this villa,
I think you look prettier.

105
00:04:27,246 --> 00:04:28,748
-Huh, seriously?
-Yeah.

106
00:04:29,248 --> 00:04:31,000
Maybe it's the vitamin from the oranges?

107
00:04:31,084 --> 00:04:35,254
Well, that's part of it, but when
you're surrounded by nature like this

108
00:04:35,338 --> 00:04:36,839
and doing fun things,

109
00:04:36,923 --> 00:04:40,843
your mind, body,
and your appearance are all healed.

110
00:04:41,511 --> 00:04:43,262
That's the ultimate beauty method.

111
00:04:43,346 --> 00:04:44,180
Right.

112
00:04:44,806 --> 00:04:48,351
Even without money,
you can become beautiful.

113
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,606
Mr. Nishigami…

114
00:04:55,066 --> 00:04:56,776
You said, "See you tomorrow"…

115
00:05:01,989 --> 00:05:04,117
The orange peels are also ready.

116
00:05:23,344 --> 00:05:25,388
Midori, what are you doing?

117
00:05:26,472 --> 00:05:27,765
I'm going out for a bit.

118
00:05:27,849 --> 00:05:28,683
Going where?

119
00:05:29,809 --> 00:05:32,854
To Mr. Nishigami's place.
We made these, after all.

120
00:05:32,937 --> 00:05:34,605
Do you know where he lives?

121
00:05:35,189 --> 00:05:36,399
I don't…

122
00:05:37,024 --> 00:05:37,942
But,

123
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:41,696
I will absolutely make him eat these.

124
00:06:53,559 --> 00:06:54,518
Hey.

125
00:06:56,479 --> 00:06:57,897
How are you doing?

126
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:00,107
Mountain God, Sea God.

127
00:07:00,816 --> 00:07:02,068
-Hello.
-What's up?

128
00:07:02,818 --> 00:07:03,986
You look gloomy.

129
00:07:07,156 --> 00:07:08,241
Could it be…

130
00:07:08,324 --> 00:07:09,617
You got scolded by our boss?

131
00:07:10,618 --> 00:07:11,953
Sorry.

132
00:07:12,745 --> 00:07:16,916
During some small talk
I may have told them everything.

133
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:18,709
It's fine.

134
00:07:18,793 --> 00:07:20,545
I'm the one at fault here.

135
00:07:23,756 --> 00:07:25,675
We're worried about you too.

136
00:07:26,759 --> 00:07:28,344
You're a Grim Reaper.

137
00:07:28,427 --> 00:07:32,515
A Reaper's job is to bear witness
to destined deaths, right?

138
00:07:33,724 --> 00:07:37,186
So, if you get too involved
with humans, things get…

139
00:07:37,270 --> 00:07:38,271
You know.

140
00:07:39,313 --> 00:07:40,231
I…

141
00:07:40,898 --> 00:07:41,941
understand that.

142
00:07:43,776 --> 00:07:44,860
What's wrong?

143
00:07:45,528 --> 00:07:47,822
-Grim Reaper--
-Mr. Nishigami!

144
00:07:51,576 --> 00:07:52,994
What's with you?

145
00:07:53,536 --> 00:07:55,037
Huh, what?

146
00:07:55,121 --> 00:07:56,038
What's wrong?

147
00:07:56,122 --> 00:07:58,040
She's cute. Huh? What's going on?

148
00:07:59,292 --> 00:08:00,668
Is she the reason?

149
00:08:02,962 --> 00:08:05,590
Mr. Nishigami,
you're avoiding me, aren't you?

150
00:08:06,173 --> 00:08:07,300
I am not.

151
00:08:07,383 --> 00:08:09,343
You are!

152
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:12,305
Here.

153
00:08:12,388 --> 00:08:14,390
The orange peels we made together.

154
00:08:15,224 --> 00:08:17,935
You stopped coming over,
so I brought them.

155
00:08:19,020 --> 00:08:20,313
They turned out delicious.

156
00:08:20,813 --> 00:08:21,856
Here.

157
00:08:23,649 --> 00:08:24,609
I don't want them.

158
00:08:24,692 --> 00:08:25,526
What?

159
00:08:26,027 --> 00:08:26,861
I'm sorry.

160
00:08:27,403 --> 00:08:28,321
I don't want them.

161
00:08:28,821 --> 00:08:30,197
Seriously?

162
00:08:30,281 --> 00:08:32,033
What is that supposed to mean?

163
00:08:35,036 --> 00:08:37,371
I thought we had finally become close.

164
00:08:38,205 --> 00:08:39,874
So it was all my misunderstanding?

165
00:08:39,957 --> 00:08:40,916
Fine then.

166
00:08:41,584 --> 00:08:42,460
I'll just…

167
00:08:43,544 --> 00:08:44,795
feed these to the fish.

168
00:10:05,418 --> 00:10:06,544
Mr. Nishigami!

169
00:10:09,422 --> 00:10:12,967
Thank you very much.
For the shower and clothes.

170
00:10:13,050 --> 00:10:14,844
Never mind that.

171
00:10:16,053 --> 00:10:18,222
Mr. Nishigami, what's the matter?

172
00:10:18,806 --> 00:10:20,683
You suddenly jumped into the sea.

173
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:22,226
But…

174
00:10:22,893 --> 00:10:24,311
The orange peels…

175
00:10:30,693 --> 00:10:31,861
Please sit down.

176
00:10:33,529 --> 00:10:34,530
Excuse me.

177
00:10:41,746 --> 00:10:42,872
Go ahead.

178
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:46,083
Thank you.

179
00:10:57,386 --> 00:10:58,804
It's very delicious.

180
00:11:02,016 --> 00:11:02,975
I'm glad.

181
00:11:14,028 --> 00:11:15,279
Mr. Nishigami…

182
00:11:17,573 --> 00:11:21,577
You haven't come by here
for the past two days.

183
00:11:23,078 --> 00:11:24,121
Could it be…

184
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,543
you have come to dislike us?

185
00:11:31,003 --> 00:11:33,130
It's not that.

186
00:11:38,636 --> 00:11:42,348
Then, please come again!
You can come anytime.

187
00:11:43,265 --> 00:11:44,266
I…

188
00:11:44,934 --> 00:11:46,227
Mr. Nishigami…

189
00:11:46,727 --> 00:11:48,771
I'm home.

190
00:11:49,605 --> 00:11:50,564
Welcome back.

191
00:11:51,065 --> 00:11:52,316
Oh, Mr. Nishigami!

192
00:11:52,399 --> 00:11:53,692
Long time no see.

193
00:11:53,776 --> 00:11:55,528
Why are you in my clothes?

194
00:11:55,611 --> 00:11:56,987
Oh, things happened.

195
00:11:57,071 --> 00:11:58,113
Let him borrow them.

196
00:11:58,197 --> 00:11:59,198
Sure, totally fine.

197
00:11:59,281 --> 00:12:01,075
Mr. Nishigami, this is perfect timing.

198
00:12:01,158 --> 00:12:02,660
We're doing a barbecue today too.

199
00:12:02,743 --> 00:12:04,370
Would you like to join us?

200
00:12:05,704 --> 00:12:06,664
I'll help.

201
00:12:23,013 --> 00:12:24,139
Mr. Nishigami!

202
00:12:26,100 --> 00:12:28,852
I want you to tell me honestly.

203
00:12:29,478 --> 00:12:32,106
How do you feel about Midori?

204
00:12:32,189 --> 00:12:33,107
What?

205
00:12:34,149 --> 00:12:37,570
You see, you're handsome,
so I think you're popular.

206
00:12:37,653 --> 00:12:40,781
But Midori is completely
unused to romance.

207
00:12:40,864 --> 00:12:43,325
That's right, unlike us.

208
00:12:44,118 --> 00:12:46,287
All right!

209
00:12:47,121 --> 00:12:48,831
All the ingredients are here.

210
00:12:48,914 --> 00:12:52,418
Let us barbecue pros get things going!

211
00:12:53,085 --> 00:12:54,461
Barbecue pros?

212
00:12:55,129 --> 00:12:57,590
It has been a whole month
since we came to this villa.

213
00:12:57,673 --> 00:13:00,634
We are practically vacation pros now.

214
00:13:00,718 --> 00:13:03,846
So, to celebrate our vacation so far,

215
00:13:04,513 --> 00:13:08,934
I would like to hold
the ultimate barbecue!

216
00:13:12,313 --> 00:13:14,690
Rinrin, you've become
really good at cooking.

217
00:13:14,773 --> 00:13:15,733
That's right.

218
00:13:15,816 --> 00:13:18,819
Before I came here,
I wouldn't even touch raw fish.

219
00:13:20,154 --> 00:13:22,781
-You've grown during the vacation.
-Yeah.

220
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:26,785
Let's see what we've got.

221
00:13:27,286 --> 00:13:29,788
Oh, it's raw squid.

222
00:13:29,872 --> 00:13:31,624
What are you doing with this?

223
00:13:31,707 --> 00:13:33,042
The squid…

224
00:13:33,959 --> 00:13:34,918
I will marinate it!

225
00:13:35,002 --> 00:13:36,170
Oh, nice.

226
00:13:36,253 --> 00:13:38,756
-That sounds good.
-We should have wine today.

227
00:13:38,839 --> 00:13:40,841
That works.

228
00:13:42,551 --> 00:13:45,846
Should we use red or white wine?

229
00:13:45,929 --> 00:13:48,849
-Maybe white.
-White wine.

230
00:13:50,601 --> 00:13:53,312
Take a look at it! It's so slimy.

231
00:13:53,395 --> 00:13:55,731
Oh, nice. Liver is tasty too.

232
00:13:55,814 --> 00:13:57,149
Nice.

233
00:13:57,232 --> 00:13:58,817
Oh, wow.

234
00:13:58,901 --> 00:14:00,361
It must feel good.

235
00:14:02,446 --> 00:14:03,489
All right.

236
00:14:04,406 --> 00:14:05,324
Let's marinate!

237
00:14:05,407 --> 00:14:06,784
Mr. Nishigami, watch closely.

238
00:14:06,867 --> 00:14:08,035
Here goes.

239
00:14:08,118 --> 00:14:09,411
Oh, my shirt suits you!

240
00:14:09,495 --> 00:14:11,163
-Thank you.
-A bit small?

241
00:14:11,246 --> 00:14:12,831
You're too ripped.

242
00:14:14,625 --> 00:14:15,709
Let's do this.

243
00:14:37,731 --> 00:14:38,732
Hey.

244
00:14:39,608 --> 00:14:42,111
About you and Midori…

245
00:14:45,489 --> 00:14:48,117
The AI said I'm in love with her.

246
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,118
I knew it.

247
00:14:49,743 --> 00:14:50,828
Really?

248
00:14:50,911 --> 00:14:56,333
It seems that, because of this vacation,
it's now easier for us to fall in love.

249
00:14:56,959 --> 00:15:02,506
So, my feelings
are just the memories of this summer.

250
00:15:04,049 --> 00:15:06,260
But I surprised myself too.

251
00:15:06,927 --> 00:15:09,263
To think that I would fall in love.

252
00:15:10,264 --> 00:15:14,518
Being able to experience this feeling
made coming here worth it.

253
00:15:15,894 --> 00:15:18,981
Then, why not make a move on Midori?

254
00:15:20,107 --> 00:15:24,945
Midori probably likes Mr. Nishigami.

255
00:15:25,904 --> 00:15:30,075
And, Mr. Nishigami is my barbecue master…

256
00:15:31,326 --> 00:15:33,787
So, I want

257
00:15:35,247 --> 00:15:37,082
the two of them to be happy.

258
00:15:37,166 --> 00:15:39,001
-You're supporting them as a couple?
-Yes.

259
00:15:39,585 --> 00:15:41,003
A new form of love, huh.

260
00:15:44,048 --> 00:15:45,966
All right, should be enough.

261
00:15:46,050 --> 00:15:47,217
How about you guys?

262
00:15:47,801 --> 00:15:48,886
-Doing good.
-Great.

263
00:15:48,969 --> 00:15:50,220
Okay.

264
00:15:51,221 --> 00:15:53,057
-Good.
-Here?

265
00:15:53,140 --> 00:15:55,142
-Right.
-Perfect.

266
00:15:55,225 --> 00:15:57,269
-Wait, I haven't spun this enough.
-Huh?

267
00:15:57,352 --> 00:15:59,813
If you need to light it, shall I help?

268
00:15:59,897 --> 00:16:01,690
It's fine. I got this.

269
00:16:07,738 --> 00:16:09,823
Nice!

270
00:16:09,907 --> 00:16:11,325
It's lit!

271
00:16:12,785 --> 00:16:15,287
-There it goes!
-Look at you all…

272
00:16:15,954 --> 00:16:20,501
Compared to when you first came here,
you feel like different people now.

273
00:16:20,584 --> 00:16:21,710
Well, yeah.

274
00:16:21,794 --> 00:16:23,504
Stay back a bit.

275
00:16:23,587 --> 00:16:25,255
Watch out.

276
00:16:25,339 --> 00:16:26,423
-Well then!
-Well then!

277
00:16:26,507 --> 00:16:27,925
Well then!

278
00:16:28,008 --> 00:16:30,761
-Cheers!
-Cheers!

279
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:33,222
So good!

280
00:16:33,889 --> 00:16:34,848
It's delicious.

281
00:16:34,932 --> 00:16:38,018
Right? I made it with summer oranges,
white wine and soda.

282
00:16:38,102 --> 00:16:40,437
You didn't put lemon sour mix
or gum syrup in it, right?

283
00:16:40,521 --> 00:16:41,688
I didn't!

284
00:16:41,772 --> 00:16:43,774
I stopped making it.
The hangovers were crazy.

285
00:16:43,857 --> 00:16:46,193
-Right?
-I never want to be hungover again!

286
00:16:46,276 --> 00:16:49,154
When you're a vacation newbie,
you tend to get overexcited, huh.

287
00:16:49,238 --> 00:16:51,240
Exactly. Konta, is it done?

288
00:16:51,323 --> 00:16:53,659
-A bit more… Oh, no, it's done!
-We can eat now?

289
00:16:53,742 --> 00:16:56,161
-Okay.
-Mr. Nishigami, drink with us.

290
00:16:56,245 --> 00:16:59,581
-Here you go.
-Thanks.

291
00:17:06,839 --> 00:17:08,006
It's delicious.

292
00:17:08,090 --> 00:17:09,424
It's like…

293
00:17:09,508 --> 00:17:11,260
Huh? What is it?

294
00:17:11,343 --> 00:17:15,097
No, I was just thinking,
a handsome guy looks good just drinking.

295
00:17:15,180 --> 00:17:17,766
Yeah. I can drink to that view.

296
00:17:17,850 --> 00:17:20,519
Hey, you two are making him uncomfortable!

297
00:17:21,270 --> 00:17:22,187
Right?

298
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:27,109
Then Midori, you don't find him handsome?

299
00:17:27,776 --> 00:17:29,611
That's not true, but…

300
00:17:29,695 --> 00:17:31,363
Oh, so you do think so.

301
00:17:31,446 --> 00:17:32,948
You think he's handsome.

302
00:17:34,366 --> 00:17:35,701
Well, yeah…

303
00:17:38,203 --> 00:17:39,121
What is this?

304
00:17:39,204 --> 00:17:40,622
Mr. Nishigami.

305
00:17:40,706 --> 00:17:42,583
You're quite a playboy, huh?

306
00:17:42,666 --> 00:17:43,792
-Hey, cut it out!
-Konta!

307
00:17:43,876 --> 00:17:46,211
Stop it! Why are you moving like that?

308
00:17:46,295 --> 00:17:47,921
Cut it out! Eat up!

309
00:17:48,005 --> 00:17:49,339
-Everyone.
-Huh?

310
00:17:49,423 --> 00:17:51,091
We have carpaccio and marinated dishes.

311
00:17:54,511 --> 00:17:56,346
I'm gonna drink too much
and get a hangover.

312
00:17:56,430 --> 00:17:57,890
I can see that.

313
00:17:58,974 --> 00:18:00,309
-Oh, Rinrin.
-Yes?

314
00:18:00,392 --> 00:18:02,686
-You want this? <i>Ajillo</i>.
-A tomato?

315
00:18:02,769 --> 00:18:05,189
I'll feed you some!

316
00:18:06,815 --> 00:18:08,358
-Yummy!
-Is it?

317
00:18:10,652 --> 00:18:13,322
I don't want to go back to Tokyo anymore.

318
00:18:13,405 --> 00:18:14,239
Me neither.

319
00:18:14,323 --> 00:18:16,491
Then, shall we all just live here?

320
00:18:16,575 --> 00:18:19,203
Maybe I should move my address here.

321
00:18:19,786 --> 00:18:24,291
I'll work part-time at a supermarket here
and earn the bare minimum.

322
00:18:24,374 --> 00:18:27,002
-Nice.
-That's awesome. Maybe I'll try farming.

323
00:18:27,085 --> 00:18:30,214
Cooking with vegetables I grew myself.
Isn't that the best?

324
00:18:30,297 --> 00:18:31,256
Yeah!

325
00:18:31,340 --> 00:18:35,886
Maybe I'll look for a remote job too.
Oh, let's install high-capacity Wi-Fi.

326
00:18:35,969 --> 00:18:37,346
Then, we can work online.

327
00:18:37,429 --> 00:18:39,598
I'll only go back to Tokyo for work.

328
00:18:39,681 --> 00:18:41,600
Otherwise, I'll just live here and drink.

329
00:18:41,683 --> 00:18:44,269
If I help out the lady next door,
I can earn 5,000 yen.

330
00:18:44,353 --> 00:18:47,356
I also got hooked on fishing,
so maybe I'll keep living here.

331
00:18:48,106 --> 00:18:50,734
I think since COVID,
more people have been living like this

332
00:18:50,817 --> 00:18:52,152
while working remotely.

333
00:18:52,236 --> 00:18:53,195
Yeah.

334
00:18:55,697 --> 00:18:56,907
Mr. Nishigami?

335
00:19:00,202 --> 00:19:01,036
It's nothing.

336
00:19:02,788 --> 00:19:03,956
Want some meat?

337
00:19:04,039 --> 00:19:05,165
I've just grilled some.

338
00:19:05,249 --> 00:19:06,166
Here you go.

339
00:19:07,125 --> 00:19:12,047
Here's the meat marinated in sauce
made from our usual summer oranges.

340
00:19:12,130 --> 00:19:13,048
Looks so good.

341
00:19:13,131 --> 00:19:14,216
Here you go.

342
00:19:14,299 --> 00:19:16,260
-Dig in.
-Thank you for the food.

343
00:19:20,347 --> 00:19:21,807
-Here.
-Thanks.

344
00:19:24,518 --> 00:19:26,853
-Hot.
-Oh, no! Are you okay?

345
00:19:32,818 --> 00:19:33,902
It's delicious.

346
00:19:34,820 --> 00:19:35,862
I'm glad.

347
00:19:39,449 --> 00:19:40,742
-Eat up, everyone.
-Yeah.

348
00:19:44,746 --> 00:19:50,002
This is what they call "chilling."

349
00:19:50,085 --> 00:19:54,673
This is so chill, yeah.

350
00:19:54,756 --> 00:19:56,466
-You get hooked on this.
-Yeah.

351
00:19:57,092 --> 00:19:59,303
Now I see why people go camping.

352
00:19:59,886 --> 00:20:03,348
But, you know, at campsites,
you have strangers nearby.

353
00:20:03,432 --> 00:20:05,767
There's no one here.
This place is the best.

354
00:20:05,851 --> 00:20:08,770
True. I love villas!

355
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:13,942
You know, I saw a street interview on TV
before, and a foreigner said,

356
00:20:14,026 --> 00:20:16,778
"Japanese people can't enjoy vacations."

357
00:20:17,362 --> 00:20:21,116
But aren't we
enjoying a perfect vacation now?

358
00:20:21,199 --> 00:20:24,745
Thanks to Mr. Nishigami,
our vacation skills have improved a lot.

359
00:20:26,038 --> 00:20:26,872
What?

360
00:20:27,539 --> 00:20:31,376
Thanks to you and this villa,
all of us have grown.

361
00:20:32,586 --> 00:20:34,379
I didn't do anything.

362
00:20:34,463 --> 00:20:37,758
At first, I only came here
to run away from reality,

363
00:20:37,841 --> 00:20:41,762
but you taught us
many things and helped us.

364
00:20:41,845 --> 00:20:45,265
So we've had a fun and safe vacation.

365
00:20:45,349 --> 00:20:48,143
Thank you for always protecting the villa.

366
00:20:49,186 --> 00:20:50,228
Keep up the good work!

367
00:20:50,312 --> 00:20:52,064
We're counting on you, Nishiyan.

368
00:20:52,147 --> 00:20:53,148
Nishiyan?

369
00:20:53,231 --> 00:20:54,316
What's with that nickname?

370
00:20:54,399 --> 00:20:56,651
He is our vacation master, after all.

371
00:20:56,735 --> 00:20:58,862
That's true. Master Nishiyan.

372
00:20:58,945 --> 00:21:00,322
Thank you, Nishiyan.

373
00:21:00,405 --> 00:21:01,573
Nishiyan.

374
00:21:04,826 --> 00:21:06,745
-Let's take a photo.
-So suddenly?

375
00:21:06,828 --> 00:21:08,121
This is the perfect time!

376
00:21:08,205 --> 00:21:09,790
Let's capture
the best moment of our lives!

377
00:21:09,873 --> 00:21:11,666
-True.
-Oh, then…

378
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:13,251
-Huh?
-I'll take it for you.

379
00:21:13,335 --> 00:21:16,046
What are you saying? You've got
to be in the photo too, Nishiyan!

380
00:21:16,129 --> 00:21:17,589
Look, there's a timer.

381
00:21:17,672 --> 00:21:20,008
Wow, your hands are thick and manly.

382
00:21:20,675 --> 00:21:21,760
Let's go, come on.

383
00:21:21,843 --> 00:21:23,678
-All right!
-There's a timer!

384
00:21:23,762 --> 00:21:25,305
-See, a timer!
-Come join us.

385
00:21:25,389 --> 00:21:28,392
-Okay. It's set for ten seconds.
-Okay!

386
00:21:28,475 --> 00:21:29,893
-You good?
-I pressed it.

387
00:21:29,976 --> 00:21:32,312
-Oops!
-What are you doing?

388
00:21:32,396 --> 00:21:35,482
Six, five, four…

389
00:21:35,565 --> 00:21:36,608
Three.

390
00:21:36,691 --> 00:21:37,526
Two.

391
00:21:37,609 --> 00:21:38,443
One.

392
00:21:41,696 --> 00:21:42,864
<i>Mr. Nishigami.</i>

393
00:21:42,948 --> 00:21:44,366
This is for you.

394
00:21:46,201 --> 00:21:47,160
I'm good…

395
00:21:48,245 --> 00:21:50,997
We can print more for ourselves.

396
00:21:51,081 --> 00:21:52,791
You should have this.

397
00:21:54,918 --> 00:21:56,336
May I?

398
00:21:57,003 --> 00:21:58,088
Of course.

399
00:22:11,435 --> 00:22:13,687
<i>A typhoon is coming soon.</i>

400
00:22:13,770 --> 00:22:17,816
<i>Because of it, a landslide will occur,</i>
<i>and that villa will be destroyed.</i>

401
00:22:18,483 --> 00:22:22,446
<i>Those five you are</i>
<i>so close with will all die.</i>

402
00:22:30,328 --> 00:22:31,454
Mr. Nishigami.

403
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:33,039
What's wrong?

404
00:22:36,668 --> 00:22:37,627
I'm fine.

405
00:22:38,336 --> 00:22:39,337
It's nothing.

406
00:22:40,630 --> 00:22:41,673
It's nothing.

407
00:23:10,076 --> 00:23:12,662
This typhoon is quite strong, huh.

408
00:23:12,746 --> 00:23:14,206
It will probably miss us.

409
00:23:14,289 --> 00:23:16,333
<i>Will Mr. Nishigami come?</i>

410
00:23:16,416 --> 00:23:17,500
It will be fine!

411
00:23:17,584 --> 00:23:19,419
<i>It's not raining that much yet.</i>

412
00:23:27,844 --> 00:23:29,429
Looks like a fun time, huh?

413
00:23:30,013 --> 00:23:30,931
Now…

414
00:23:31,014 --> 00:23:32,807
This is your final warning.

415
00:23:33,767 --> 00:23:34,768
<i>Mr. Nishigami?</i>

416
00:23:35,352 --> 00:23:36,686
Such a thing is impossible!

417
00:23:36,770 --> 00:23:38,355
Listen up, Reaper.

418
00:23:38,438 --> 00:23:41,191
You'll be erased like sand by Lady Yomi.

419
00:23:41,775 --> 00:23:44,236
<i>Don't forget. You are a Grim Reaper.</i>

420
00:23:45,153 --> 00:23:46,112
Subtitle translation by: Nix S.

